            <div type="edition" xml:space="preserve" xml:lang="la" resp="#AV">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/><persName type="divine" key="apolloBelenusAugustus"><name>Apollini</name>
                    <lb n="2"/><name>Beleno</name> <name><expan><abbr>Aug</abbr><ex>usto</ex></expan></name></persName>
                    <lb n="3"/>in honorem
                    <lb n="4"/><persName type="attested"><name><expan><abbr>C</abbr><ex>ai</ex></expan></name> <name>Petti</name> <name><expan><abbr>C</abbr><ex>ai</ex></expan></name></persName> <expan><abbr>f</abbr><ex>ili</ex></expan> <persName type="attested"><name><expan><abbr>Pal</abbr><ex>atina</ex></expan></name>
                    <lb n="5"/><name>Philtati</name></persName> <expan><abbr>eq</abbr><ex>uo</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>p</abbr><ex>ublico</ex></expan> 
                    <lb n="6"/><expan><abbr>praef</abbr><ex>ecti</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>aed</abbr><ex>ilicia</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>pot</abbr><ex>estate</ex></expan>
                    <lb n="7"/><expan><abbr>praef</abbr><ex>ecti</ex></expan> et patroni
                    <lb n="8"/>collegiorum
                    <lb n="9"/><expan><abbr>fabr</abbr><ex>um</ex></expan> et <expan><abbr>cent</abbr><ex>onariorum</ex></expan>
                    <lb n="10"/><persName type="attested"><name>Diocles</name></persName> <expan><abbr>lib</abbr><ex>ertus</ex></expan> 
                    <lb n="11"/>donum dedit
                    <lb n="12"/><expan><abbr>l</abbr><ex>ocus</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>d</abbr><ex>atus</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>d</abbr><ex>ecreto</ex></expan> <expan><abbr>d</abbr><ex>ecurionum</ex></expan>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus">
                <listApp>
                    <app><note>Text from EDR</note></app>
                </listApp>
            </div>
            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>To Apollo Belenus Augustus. In honor of Gaius Pettus Philtatus, son of Gaius, of tribe Palatina, with the public horse, prefect with aedilician power, prefect and patron of the college of carpenters and textile dealers. 
                    Diocles a freedman gave this gift. This location was given by decree of the decurions.
                </p>
